      "writtenOn": "2022-08-23T19:18:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this is indeed needed, then we need a better name, otherwise users will have to dig through the code to figure out what check is being skipped.\n\nThat said, what is the harm in re-triggering interrupt unconditionally. Daniel, any opinion here? It looks we are dealing with INT-x here which have level-triggered semantics as opposed to edge.",
      "revId": "e18bea0cf3f204a61d8bed1c5f13fc60591aea3b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c39501c4_cb7941f7",
        "filename": "devices/src/virtio/interrupt.rs",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
