        "id": 1572669
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-23T19:42:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Removing the check entirely might be okay, but it should be backed up by benchmarks.\n\nIt might make a difference in cases where a device processes many requests in a batch and calls `Queue::trigger_interrupt()` repeatedly, although if the guest driver uses `VIRTIO_RING_F_EVENT_IDX` for interrupt suppression, it might not matter that much.",
      "parentUuid": "0195cdfe_36f174fb",
      "revId": "e18bea0cf3f204a61d8bed1c5f13fc60591aea3b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f51cd943_1ccf93c5",
        "filename": "devices/src/virtio/interrupt.rs",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 66,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572669
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-23T19:42:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should probably still set the requested bits in `interrupt_status`, since this skips the `fetch_or` below. Otherwise the interrupt handler will not know what caused the interrupt (used ring or config change). This could probably be merged into the block below:\n\n```\nif self.interrupt_status.fetch_or(...) \u003d\u003d 0 || self.skip_check {\n    self.interrupt_evt.trigger();\n}\n```",
      "revId": "e18bea0cf3f204a61d8bed1c5f13fc60591aea3b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
